{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"checkIsolated"},{"kind":"text","text":"()"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"During executor comparison, the Swift concurrency runtime attempts to compare"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"current and expected executors in a few ways (including “complex” equality"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"between executors (see "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/SerialExecutor\/isSameExclusiveExecutionContext(other:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"), and if all"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"those checks fail, this method is invoked on the expected executor."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This method MUST crash if it is unable to prove that the current execution"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"context belongs to this executor. At this point usual executor comparison would"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"have already failed, though the executor may have some external tracking of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"threads it owns, and may be able to prove isolation nevertheless."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A default implementation is provided that unconditionally crashes the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"program, and prevents calling code from proceeding with potentially"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not thread-safe execution."}]},{"type":"aside","style":"warning","name":"Warning","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This method must crash and halt program execution if unable"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to prove the isolation of the calling context."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/SerialExecutor"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Last resort “fallback” isolation check, called when the concurrency runtime"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is comparing executors e.g. during "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"assumeIsolated()"},{"type":"text","text":" and is unable to prove"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"serial equivalence between the expected (this object), and the current executor."}],"metadata":{"externalID":"s:Scf13checkIsolatedyyF","title":"checkIsolated()","symbolKind":"method","platforms":[{"beta":false,"name":"iOS","deprecated":false,"introducedAt":"8.0","unavailable":false},{"beta":false,"name":"iPadOS","deprecated":false,"introducedAt":"8.0","unavailable":false},{"beta":false,"name":"Mac Catalyst","deprecated":false,"introducedAt":"13.0","unavailable":false},{"beta":false,"name":"macOS","deprecated":false,"introducedAt":"10.10","unavailable":false},{"beta":false,"name":"tvOS","deprecated":false,"introducedAt":"9.0","unavailable":false},{"beta":false,"name":"visionOS","deprecated":false,"introducedAt":"1.0","unavailable":false},{"beta":false,"name":"watchOS","deprecated":false,"introducedAt":"2.0","unavailable":false}],"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"checkIsolated","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"()","kind":"text"}],"roleHeading":"Instance Method","role":"symbol","required":true,"modules":[{"name":"Swift","relatedModules":[]}]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swift\/serialexecutor\/checkisolated()"]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/SerialExecutor\/checkIsolated()","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"defaultImplementationsSections":[{"anchor":"SerialExecutor-Implementations","title":"SerialExecutor Implementations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/SerialExecutor\/checkIsolated()-76lg2"]}],"references":{"doc://com.apple.Swift/documentation/Swift/SerialExecutor":{"url":"\/documentation\/swift\/serialexecutor","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A service that executes jobs."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SerialExecutor"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/SerialExecutor","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SerialExecutor"}],"title":"SerialExecutor"},"doc://com.apple.Swift/documentation/Swift":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swift","role":"collection","title":"Swift","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift","abstract":[{"text":"Build apps using a powerful open language.","type":"text"}]},"doc://com.apple.Swift/documentation/Swift/SerialExecutor/isSameExclusiveExecutionContext(other:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/swift\/serialexecutor\/issameexclusiveexecutioncontext(other:)","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"If this executor has complex equality semantics, and the runtime needs to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"compare two executors, it will first attempt the usual pointer-based"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"equality \/ check, \/ and if it fails it will compare the types of both"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"executors, if they are the same, \/ it will finally invoke this method,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"attempt to let the executor itself decide \/ if this and the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"other"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"executor represent the same serial, exclusive, isolation context."}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/SerialExecutor\/isSameExclusiveExecutionContext(other:)","required":true,"type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"isSameExclusiveExecutionContext"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"other"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","text":"Bool","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"defaultImplementations":2,"title":"isSameExclusiveExecutionContext(other:)"},"doc://com.apple.Swift/documentation/Swift/SerialExecutor/checkIsolated()-76lg2":{"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"checkIsolated"},{"kind":"text","text":"()"}],"abstract":[],"title":"checkIsolated()","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/SerialExecutor\/checkIsolated()-76lg2","url":"\/documentation\/swift\/serialexecutor\/checkisolated()-76lg2"},"doc://com.apple.Swift/documentation/Swift/SerialExecutor/checkIsolated()":{"url":"\/documentation\/swift\/serialexecutor\/checkisolated()","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Last resort “fallback” isolation check, called when the concurrency runtime"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is comparing executors e.g. during "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"assumeIsolated()"},{"type":"text","text":" and is unable to prove"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"serial equivalence between the expected (this object), and the current executor."}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/SerialExecutor\/checkIsolated()","required":true,"type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"k